    "body": "This can be simplified a bit and made more consistent with other cases of \"whose form owner\" in the spec. How about:\n\n> For each form-associated element _element_ whose form\n  owner is removedNode, in tree order:\n> 1. If ... then reset the form owner ...\n\nSome existing cases don't use \"in tree order\" and it won't make a difference, but it's better to have it in case some future steps do make the order observable.",
